   "q": "Sharp (♯)",
   "a": "A sharp raises a note to the very next key on the right. D sharp is the black key just right of D. The famous opening simply rocks a half step: E, D sharp, E."
  },
  {
   "staff": {
    "notes": [
     69,
     68,
     69
    ]
   },
   "q": "A minor, and why there is a G sharp",
   "a": "This piece uses the white keys but treats A as home, not C. That is A minor, the darker twin of C major. The G sharp is borrowed: being only a half step below A, it pulls the ear back home."
  },
  {
   "staff": {
    "notes": [
